    "physical_description": "WARP: white wool; Z2S; 24 threads per inch (90 per dm).\r\n\r\nWEFT:  brown wool; Z spun; unplied; 2 parallel threads per shoot; 2 shoots after each row of knots; 21 knots per inch (81 per dm).\r\n\r\nPILE: wool; 8 colours: red, orange, dark green, dark blue, blue, pink, brown, white; asymmetrical knot open to the right and tied around 2 threads; 252 knots per sq. inch (3645 knots per sq. dm).\r\n\r\nSIDE FINISH: 3 cords overcast with red wool.\r\n\r\nEND FINISH: Lower: cut.  Upper: plain weave with red and then white woollen weft, turned and stitched.  Red and green wool plait sewn along fold but bits missing.\r\n\r\nDESIGN: Field: red ground with two bands of three stepped and hooked guls, one above the other.  In the centre of each, a pink and blue quartered hexagon within a larger rectangle framed alternately pink and red.  The rectangle is also quartered, with dark green bottom left and top right corners, and white in inner top left and inner lower right.  There is a central band with two lozenge arrangements of eight blue-outlined, small rectangles each containing a white star and framing a geometric, hooked motif outlined in brown.  Similar upper and lower bands are partially evident.\r\n\r\nMain border: rectangles with contrasting star-like motif and separated (upper and lower) by narrow blocks of red and (sides) by multi-coloured bands.\r\n\r\nInner and outer borders: pink ground (lower parts have red ground) altnerating with white and red flowerheads outlined in dark green.\r\n\r\nUpper border: row of blue, dark green, brown and white horns rise directly from the outer border.\r\n\r\nApron: pile 19 cms. in depth; diagonal row of alternating dark blue and dark green sprigs with white flowers - the dark blue infilled with red or orange and the dark green",
